 "answer": "Ollama on Windows writes its server log to:\n\n**`%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Ollama\\server.log`**\n\nThe full path is usually `C:\\Users\\<your-username>\\AppData\\Local\\Ollama\\server.log`.\n\nTo open the folder, press Win+R, enter `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Ollama`, and open `server.log`. Or in PowerShell:\n\n```powershell\nnotepad \"$env:LOCALAPPDATA\\Ollama\\server.log\"\n```\n\nThe same folder also holds `app.log` (logs from the Ollama tray app) and `upgrade.log`. I believe older server logs are rotated into numbered files such as `server-1.log`, but I'm not certain of the exact naming, so check the folder if you need an older entry.",
